hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18021","Muawiyah ibn Hisham Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from al-Shabi, he said: Muti ibn al-Aswad said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest: It is not proper that a Qurashi be killed in captivity after this day of his."
"18022","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Zakariya, Amir narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muti from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: No Qurashi shall be killed in captivity after today. And none of the disobedient of Quraysh attained Islam except Muti, and his name was Asi, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Muti."
"18023","Waki narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us from Amir from Abdullah ibn Muti from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of the conquest of Makkah: No Qurashi shall be killed in captivity after today until the Day of Resurrection."
"18024","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar from Amir al-Shabi from Abdullah ibn Muti ibn al-Aswad, brother of Banu Adi ibn Kab, from his father Muti, and his name was al-As, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Muti, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ordered the killing of this group in Makkah saying: Makkah shall not be raided after this year ever, and no Qurashi shall be killed in captivity after this year ever."
